-## Full integration work still outstanding
-
-Preferred architecture to evaluate against the stock trace:
-
-1. **Bluetooth transport (`system/bt`)**: add a device-gated, narrowly scoped FM
-   endpoint which submits commands through Fluoride's existing HCI queue. Keep
-   command credits, completion ownership, Bluetooth power/lifetime, client
-   death, timeouts, and concurrent SCO use under one owner. Authenticate clients
-   and restrict operations; never expose an arbitrary HCI injector over TCP.
-   Opening `/dev/ttySAC0` independently while Bluetooth owns it is not safe.
-2. **FM backend/app**: provide a separate HCI backend implementing the Lineage
